{
  "title": "Rescrape polling task keeps running after the recipe detail view \
is dismissed",
  "description": "`Ramekin/RecipeDetailViewRescrape.swift` polls \
`getScrapeStatus` in a detached `Task` that runs for up to 120s. If the user \
backs out of the recipe before the scrape completes, the task is not cancelled \
— it continues hitting the server, and its `await MainActor.run { ... }` still \
flips `@State` on a view that no longer exists (noisy warnings at minimum, \
risk of unexpected state writes). Store the `Task` as `@State` and cancel it \
from `.onDisappear`, or move the polling into a `.task(id:)` on the view which \
SwiftUI cancels automatically.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-04-17T12:00:00-07:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-04-17T12:00:00-07:00",
}
